# Default Surface Only

When styling elevated content (cards, panels, sections, grouped UI), always use the **default surface** token. Do not use secondary or tertiary surface levels.

## Surface hierarchy

| Layer | Token | Tailwind | Use for |
|-------|-------|----------|---------|
| Canvas | `background` | `bg-background` | Page/shell background only |
| Content | `surface` | `bg-surface` | Cards, panels, sidebars, modals, any elevated UI |
| ~~Nested~~ | ~~`surface-secondary`~~ | ~~`bg-surface-secondary`~~ | **Do not use** |
| ~~Nested~~ | ~~`surface-tertiary`~~ | ~~`bg-surface-tertiary`~~ | **Do not use** |

## Rules

- Use `bg-surface` and `text-surface-foreground` for all elevated surfaces.
- Use `bg-background` only for the page canvas behind content.
- Never use `bg-surface-secondary`, `bg-surface-tertiary`, or their foreground variants.
- Never pass `secondary` or `tertiary` as a surface variant on components.
- Prefer `border border-separator` or spacing (`gap`, `p-*`) to separate nested content instead of a darker surface layer.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — secondary/tertiary surfaces
<div className="bg-surface-secondary rounded-lg p-4">...</div>
<div className="bg-surface-tertiary">...</div>
<Card variant="secondary">...</Card>

// ✅ GOOD — default surface only
<div className="bg-surface text-surface-foreground rounded-lg p-4">...</div>
<Card>...</Card>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — stacking surface levels for nesting
<div className="bg-surface p-4">
  <div className="bg-surface-secondary rounded-md p-3">...</div>
</div>

// ✅ GOOD — same surface, use border or spacing for grouping
<div className="bg-surface p-4">
  <div className="rounded-md border border-separator p-3">...</div>
</div>
```
